# مفاتيح (Mafati7) — Project Conventions

## Project Overview
Chrome Extension (Manifest V3) — Secure password manager vault with encrypted credential storage, autofill, multi-language support (i18n), and RTL-first design.

## Branch Naming
- `feat/<short-description>` — new features (e.g., `feat/inline-credentials-minimize`)
- `fix/<short-description>` — bug fixes (e.g., `fix/crypto-normalize-payload-format`)
- `docs/<short-description>` — documentation (e.g., `docs/ai-reflection-improvement-tasks`)
- `codex/<short-description>` — AI-generated exploration branches
- Use kebab-case and keep descriptions concise.

## CSS Naming Conventions
Use BEM-like naming throughout:

### Pattern
- **Block**: single name, e.g., `.site-row`, `.vault-gate`, `.cred-pair`, `.empty-state`
- **Element**: block name + `__` + element name, e.g., `.app__header`, `.vault-gate__icon`, `.cred-pair__login`, `.empty-state__icon`
- **Modifier**: block/element name + `--` + modifier name, e.g., `.primary--glow`, `.btn--outline`
- **State classes**: use regular class, e.g., `.dragging`, `.show`

### CSS Variables
Use `--` custom properties in `:root` for all design tokens:
- Colors: `--bg-*`, `--text-*`, `--border-*`, `--accent-*`, `--danger`, `--success`, `--warning`
- Radii: `--radius-sm`, `--radius-md`, `--radius-lg`, `--radius-pill`
- Shadows: `--shadow-glow-sm`, `--shadow-glow-md`, `--shadow-elevate`

### Key CSS Files
- `src/popup/popup.css` — popup UI styles
- `src/options/options.css` — settings page styles

## i18n (Internationalization)

### Supported Languages
| Code | Language   | Direction |
|------|------------|-----------|
| ar   | العربية    | rtl       |
| en   | English    | ltr       |
| fr   | Français   | ltr       |
| es   | Español    | ltr       |
| hi   | हिन्दी     | ltr       |
| zh   | 中文       | ltr       |

### Translation File
- **Location**: `src/common/i18n.js`
- All translations live in the `TRANSLATIONS` object with camelCase keys
- Example key pattern: `appName`, `vaultLocked`, `unlockBtn`, `entriesCount`, `copiedUrl`

### Key Naming
- Group by feature/section (e.g., `appName`, `vaultLocked`, `entriesCount`, `dialog*`, `export*`, `import*`)
- Use camelCase
- For placeholder/contextual keys: `{placeholder}` syntax (e.g., `entriesCount: "{count} entries"`)

### HTML Attributes
- `data-i18n="keyName"` — translates `textContent`
- `data-i18n-placeholder="keyName"` — translates `placeholder`
- `data-i18n-title="keyName"` — translates `title`
- `data-i18n-value="keyName"` — translates `value`
- `data-replace-{name}="value"` — for dynamic placeholder replacement

### Usage in JS
```js
import { t, initI18n, setLanguage, saveAndApplyLanguage } from "../common/i18n.js";
t("keyName", { placeholder: "value" });
```

### Default Language
The default language is Arabic (`"ar"`). Language preference is stored in `chrome.storage.local` under the key `app_language`.

## Event Delegation Pattern

### Main File
- `src/popup/popup-events.js`

### Pattern
1. Export `initEvents(refs)` which stores DOM references and calls `wireEvents()`
2. `wireEvents()` attaches listeners to parent containers (not individual elements)
3. Use `event.target.closest(".selector")` to identify which element was clicked
4. Check for specific action buttons within the row using `event.target.closest()`

### ⚠️ Container Boundary Rule
Event delegation does NOT cross container boundaries. If a new DOM container
is added (e.g., `#minimizedList` as a sibling of `#websiteList`), it MUST have
its own `.addEventListener()` calls in `wireEvents()`. Events from children of
one container will NOT bubble to listeners on a different container.

### Example
```js
function wireEvents() {
  siteList.addEventListener("click", onListClick);
  siteList.addEventListener("dblclick", onListDblClick);
}

async function onListClick(event) {
  const row = event.target.closest(".site-row");
  if (!row) return;
  if (event.target.closest(".open-site")) { /* handle open */ }
  if (event.target.closest(".edit-site")) { /* handle edit */ }
}
```

### Action Buttons Convention
- `.open-site` — open URL in new tab
- `.edit-site` — open edit dialog
- `.delete-site` — delete entry
- `.cred-pair__lock` — toggle password visibility
- `.cred-pair__fill` — autofill credentials
- `.minimize-site` — minimize site row to bottom
- `.minimized-site` — dblclick to restore

## RTL Support

### Requirements
- All major layout uses logical properties where possible (`margin-inline-start`, `padding-inline-end`)
- `[dir="rtl"]` CSS overrides for elements that need explicit RTL behavior
- Credential data (`cred-pair__login`, `cred-pair__password-reveal`) must stay `direction: ltr` even in RTL mode to preserve login/password text direction
- `document.documentElement.dir` is set dynamically by `i18n.js` based on the current language
- Bidi-isolate any LTR content inside RTL layout

### CSS Example
```css
[dir="rtl"] .app,
[dir="rtl"] .vault-gate,
[dir="rtl"] .modal__content { direction: rtl; text-align: right; }

.cred-pair__login {
  direction: ltr;
  text-align: left;
}
```

## Project Structure
```
├── popup.html              # Popup entry HTML
├── options.html            # Settings page HTML
├── manifest.json           # Extension manifest (MV3)
├── src/
│   ├── background/
│   │   └── service-worker.js
│   ├── common/
│   │   ├── constants.js    # STORAGE_KEYS, DEFAULT_FIELD_KEYWORDS
│   │   ├── crypto.js       # Encryption/decryption (salt + verifier pattern)
│   │   ├── i18n.js         # Translation module
│   │   ├── models.js       # Data model helpers
│   │   └── storage.js      # Chrome storage wrappers
│   ├── content/
│   │   └── autofill-content.js  # Content script for autofill
│   ├── options/
│   │   ├── options.css
│   │   └── options-main.js
│   └── popup/
│       ├── popup.css
│       ├── popup-main.js
│       ├── popup-events.js       # Event delegation (wireEvents)
│       ├── popup-state.js        # Mutable state object
│       ├── popup-dom.js          # DOM element creation
│       ├── popup-render.js       # Rendering and toast
│       ├── popup-dialog.js       # Dialog management
│       ├── popup-collapse.js     # Collapse/expand list
│       ├── popup-drag.js         # Drag-and-drop reorder
│       └── popup-vault.js        # Vault unlock/lock logic
```

## Storage Keys
Defined in `src/common/constants.js`:
- `credential_websites` — encrypted websites list
- `field_keywords` — autofill field detection keywords
- `master_salt` — crypto salt
- `master_verifier` — master password verifier
- `app_language` — saved language preference

## General Coding Conventions
- ES modules (`type="module"` in HTML, `import`/`export` in JS)
- `async/await` for all async operations
- Try-catch blocks around crypto operations (decryption can fail)
- Toast messages use `showToast(listMessage, text, type)` where type is `"success"`, `"warning"`, or `"muted"`
- Chrome Extension APIs: `chrome.storage.local`, `chrome.tabs`, `chrome.runtime`

## ⚠️ Tool Usage: `filesystem__directory_tree` Restriction

**NEVER** call `filesystem__directory_tree` on large directories (project root, `.git`, `node_modules`, `dist`, `build`, `doc`, `coverage`, `vendor`, etc.) — it recursively enumerates ALL files and subdirectories into a single JSON structure, causing timeouts or crashes when thousands of files are present.

### ✅ Safe Alternatives

| Task | Use Instead |
|------|-------------|
| **List contents of a single directory** (non-recursive) | `filesystem__list_directory("/path")` |
| **List with file sizes** (non-recursive) | `filesystem__list_directory_with_sizes("/path")` |
| **Find files matching a pattern** (recursive but filtered) | `filesystem__search_files("/project/root", "**/*.js")` with `excludePatterns` |
| **Quick look at project structure** (limited depth) | `filesystem__directory_tree("/project/root", { excludePatterns: ["node_modules/*", ".git/*", "dist/*"] })` with explicit exclusions |
| **Specific file info** | `filesystem__get_file_info("/path/to/file")` |
| **Shell-level exploration** (complex queries) | `run_commands({ commands: ["find src -name '*.js' | head -50"] })` |

### ⚡ Golden Rule
- **First try** `filesystem__list_directory` (flat, one level) to see what's in a directory.
- **If you need recursive search**, use `filesystem__search_files` with a specific glob pattern — it returns flat paths, not a tree.
- **Only use `filesystem__directory_tree`** on small, well-known directories (e.g., a single `src/components/` directory you already know is small), and **always** pass `excludePatterns` for any large subdirectories.
- **Never** call it on the project root, `.git`, `node_modules`, `dist`, `build`, `doc`, or any path you haven't inspected first with `filesystem__list_directory`.
